    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen attempting to build the dev version of `h5py` with Python 3.15 + Limited API, Cython generates code which includes `PyObject_CallFinalizerFromDealloc`, which isn't part of the Limited API\n```\ncd h5py\nH5PY_LIMITED_API=1 uv build -p 3.15\nabi3audit dist/*cp315*.whl\n```\n\nInspecting the generated code itself reveals that the following line is very likely the culprit:\nhttps://github.com/cython/cython/blob/0e66fb28b1cbcb8f508053d56bbbbbcf6ece6c1c/Cython/Compiler/ModuleNode.py#L2066\n\nbut this is as far as I can stretch it for now. Hopefully the defect is actually obvious\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n_No response_\n\n### OS\n\nany\n\n### Python version\n\n3.15.0rc1\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
